.TH BIOME 1 "September 2026" "biome" "Biome Wayland compositor"
.SH NAME
biome \- fixed-policy Wayland compositor for Forest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biome
.RB [ \-s
.IR "startup command" ]
.br
.B biome
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biome
is an opinionated, single-policy Wayland compositor built on wlroots. It is
not user-configurable like sway or river; window and output policy is fixed
in code. It owns the seat and DRM output and is normally the top-level
process of a session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " command"
Fork and exec
.I command
as a child process once Biome's Wayland socket is live, inheriting
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY .
Used to start a session's own process (see
.BR forest-session (1)).
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/biome/conf.d/*.conf
.RS
System-wide defaults, read in filename order; typically installed by a
desktop shell package.
.RE
.I ~/.config/Biome/Biome.conf
.RS
Per-user output layout and fade settings. A key set here overrides the
same key from
.IR /etc/biome/conf.d .
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1),
.BR forest-session (1)
